# DAWg's tests: the checks below don't fit test code, so they're off here. Tests seed their noise with constants so
# runs repeat; they read optionals a REQUIRE has just checked; they work out sample counts from small constants
# (block * blockSize) and halve integer beats; they keep fixtures in file-scope statics, step through values in
# floating-point loops, grow small result vectors in loops, and give their small test rigs non-const helpers. Exact
# floating-point comparisons are on purpose too: tests/CMakeLists.txt turns Clang's -Wfloat-equal off for test
# sources. All other checks still apply.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed,
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast,
  -bugprone-integer-division,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -bugprone-float-loop-counter,
  -performance-inefficient-vector-operation,
  -readability-make-member-function-const
